1
00:00:00,375 --> 00:00:02,375
- Hey, Pen!
- Huh? What is it?

2
00:00:02,375 --> 00:00:04,500
Well, I was thinking about some stuff,

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:07,666
and I thought of something that
might be a really cool coincidence!

4
00:00:07,666 --> 00:00:09,041
And, what would that be?

5
00:00:09,041 --> 00:00:12,833
I wonder what would happen if you took
the first spoken word of the first episode,

6
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:15,250
the second spoken word of the second episode,

7
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:18,916
all the way until the 25th spoken
word of the 25th episode...

8
00:00:18,916 --> 00:00:21,791
- Yeah?
- ...and lined up those words to make a message.

9
00:00:22,041 --> 00:00:23,375
W-what would you get?

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,916
I don't know, probably nothing.

11
00:00:26,166 --> 00:00:32,791
[INTRO PLAYS]

12
00:00:32,791 --> 00:00:34,166
Subtitles: TAFFYMARZI

13
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,958
Announcer:
22 cakes have come and gone,
but none of them are nearly as

14
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:40,791
magnificent as the Grand Cake.

15
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:43,666
Bubble:
That is seriously a hideous cake!

16
00:00:43,666 --> 00:00:46,625
Really, Bubble? When did I say you
were allowed to speak?

17
00:00:47,125 --> 00:00:49,000
Never. But let's do Cake at Stake!

18
00:00:50,083 --> 00:00:50,750
♪ Da-da-da-da-da-da ♪

19
00:00:59,416 --> 00:01:00,791
♪ The points are gone ♪

20
00:01:00,791 --> 00:01:02,625
♪ We are free of them now ♪

21
00:01:02,625 --> 00:01:03,958
♪ But we look on ♪

22
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,083
♪ To the moment that we see ♪

23
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:09,375
♪ The next slice of cake ♪

24
00:01:09,625 --> 00:01:11,833
♪ A step closer to the prize ♪

25
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:12,541
♪ Brought on by- ♪

26
00:01:12,541 --> 00:01:13,708
Everyone:
Cake at Stake!

27
00:01:13,875 --> 00:01:15,333
Aw, seriously?!

28
00:02:06,416 --> 00:02:08,958
We're going to release the eliminated contestants.

29
00:02:08,958 --> 00:02:10,083
Leafy:
No! Don't do that!

30
00:02:10,083 --> 00:02:10,708
Why not?

31
00:02:10,833 --> 00:02:11,625
Firey:
You dunno?

32
00:02:11,875 --> 00:02:15,583
After years of seclusion, those...
those creatures have gone INSANE!

33
00:02:15,666 --> 00:02:16,125
Announcer:
Too late.

34
00:02:17,416 --> 00:02:18,833
See? They're perfectly fi-

35
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:20,458
Ough!

36
00:02:20,583 --> 00:02:22,041
Are you all ready for the æ?

37
00:02:22,166 --> 00:02:23,750
Ae? What's the æ?

38
00:02:23,875 --> 00:02:26,125
I said æ. æ. ææææ.

39
00:02:26,375 --> 00:02:29,833
Well, I guess I'm unable to
pronounce the 'ay sound anymore.

40
00:02:29,833 --> 00:02:32,583
You mean the K sound?
You can't pronounce the K sound!

41
00:02:32,583 --> 00:02:34,125
Whatever, now be 'uiet.

42
00:02:34,125 --> 00:02:36,958
Thanks a lot, Flower.
You've messed up the Announcer!

43
00:02:37,166 --> 00:02:38,291
O'ay, moving on.

44
00:02:38,708 --> 00:02:42,583
The... uhm... pastry, is all of the previous
pastries meshed together.

45
00:02:42,666 --> 00:02:43,666
Oh wow!

46
00:02:43,666 --> 00:02:46,583
Auuuuuuuuugh...

47
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:48,125
Leafy, stop salivating.

48
00:02:48,583 --> 00:02:51,166
Firey, you too, or you'll destroy yourself.

49
00:02:51,375 --> 00:02:53,041
Ahhhhh... GAH!

50
00:02:53,375 --> 00:02:54,416
Hurry up, already!

51
00:02:54,416 --> 00:02:58,125
So the person who got the most votes,
will get this entire pastry,

52
00:02:58,125 --> 00:02:59,625
along with Dream Island as well.

53
00:03:00,708 --> 00:03:04,708
We got 870 votes, which means
there will be no Season Two.

54
00:03:04,791 --> 00:03:05,333
Aww!

55
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,375
Before we announce the winner of BFDI,

56
00:03:08,375 --> 00:03:11,208
let's see who the eliminated people want to win.

57
00:03:11,625 --> 00:03:14,666
Well, Leafy's killed me, Bubble's killed me,
and Firey's killed me,

58
00:03:14,666 --> 00:03:16,125
so I don't think any of them should win.

59
00:03:16,125 --> 00:03:19,333
But if we absolutely had to choose
one of them, who would it be?

60
00:03:19,333 --> 00:03:20,916
Leafy! Because she's a plant.

61
00:03:20,958 --> 00:03:21,583
Announcer:
Spongy.

62
00:03:21,583 --> 00:03:22,250
Leafy!

63
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:26,041
Leafy, 'cause Firey's deadly
and Bubble's fun to kill.

64
00:03:26,041 --> 00:03:26,750
Leaveh...

65
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:27,375
Leafy!

66
00:03:27,375 --> 00:03:29,083
Wow, Pin! You remembered our-

67
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,041
Pin, alliance, remember?

68
00:03:31,041 --> 00:03:31,583
Pin:
Oh yeah.

69
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:32,583
Of course!

70
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:35,541
And Needy, you vote for Leafy, too! Right?

71
00:03:36,041 --> 00:03:38,125
Don't call me Needy! But no.

72
00:03:38,125 --> 00:03:38,750
Then who?

73
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:39,500
Firey!

74
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,375
Announcer:
Teardrop, are you going to vote?

75
00:03:45,458 --> 00:03:50,125
Leafy, and I realize all of the finalists
weigh less than 1/10 of an ounce.

76
00:03:50,333 --> 00:03:52,833
I vote Leafy, definitely not Firey.

77
00:03:52,833 --> 00:03:53,750
Me too!

78
00:03:53,750 --> 00:03:55,250
OMG! Bubble!

79
00:03:56,375 --> 00:03:57,250
Leafy.

80
00:03:57,250 --> 00:03:58,041
Leafy!

81
00:03:58,041 --> 00:03:58,958
Leafy.

82
00:03:58,958 --> 00:04:00,041
Uhh, Bubble.

83
00:04:00,208 --> 00:04:02,250
LEAFY! Leafy! Leafy, I mean Leafy!

84
00:04:02,416 --> 00:04:03,250
[leaves rustle]

85
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:04,250
Leafy!

86
00:04:04,291 --> 00:04:04,666
Bleh!

87
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,208
Leafy wins by a 15:2 vote.

88
00:04:07,208 --> 00:04:07,875
Yay!

89
00:04:07,875 --> 00:04:09,875
But that doesn't mean you win Dream Island.

90
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,208
Then who wins Dream Island?

91
00:04:11,208 --> 00:04:13,500
Whoever got the most votes from the viewers.

92
00:04:14,375 --> 00:04:18,375
Bubble, I'm sorry, but you only received 228 votes,

93
00:04:18,375 --> 00:04:21,166
so you don't win, but you played a great game.

94
00:04:21,166 --> 00:04:22,750
Announcer:
You were a wonderful 'ontestant.

95
00:04:22,750 --> 00:04:24,500
Oh, do I at least get a prize?

96
00:04:24,666 --> 00:04:25,875
You get one 'ashew.

97
00:04:25,875 --> 00:04:26,625
Bless you!

98
00:04:26,625 --> 00:04:28,125
No, I said 'ashew.

99
00:04:28,125 --> 00:04:29,958
Wow, you must be allergic to something.

100
00:04:29,958 --> 00:04:31,500
'Ashew. 'Ashew. 'Ashew.

101
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:33,583
Maybe the announcer is allergic to this cashew.

102
00:04:33,958 --> 00:04:35,041
Here, you can have it, Bubble!

103
00:04:35,041 --> 00:04:35,958
YOYLECAKE!

104
00:04:35,958 --> 00:04:38,041
So the winner is either Firey or Leafy.

105
00:04:38,041 --> 00:04:41,458
Firey, y-you're such a great friend.
I'll be happy if either of us win.

106
00:04:41,458 --> 00:04:42,541
Let's show the votes.

107
00:04:43,375 --> 00:04:45,625
What? No drumroll? Why not?

108
00:04:45,666 --> 00:04:46,458
Budget 'uts.

109
00:04:46,458 --> 00:04:48,708
- Uhhh...
- I mean budget downsizings.

110
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,458
So, Firey, you win.

111
00:04:50,666 --> 00:04:51,375
Yeah-hah!

112
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:52,750
Huhel...

113
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,625
Before I give you Dream Island,

114
00:04:54,625 --> 00:04:58,166
I want to than' the viewers for viewing,
and the voters for voting.

115
00:04:58,708 --> 00:05:04,083
Than's go out to jaysillyboy for voting the first ever vote,
cheryblosen for the last ever vote,

116
00:05:04,083 --> 00:05:07,166
and the 6,814 votes in between.

117
00:05:07,166 --> 00:05:07,916
Hurry up!

118
00:05:07,916 --> 00:05:09,083
Okay, let's go.

119
00:05:09,666 --> 00:05:12,833
First, choose the people who should
be allowed onto the island.

120
00:05:12,833 --> 00:05:13,500
Hmmm...

121
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:14,416
Choose us!

122
00:05:14,416 --> 00:05:16,083
Yeah, choose us! Choose us!

123
00:05:16,083 --> 00:05:16,750
Okay!

124
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:17,750
YOYLECAKE!

125
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:20,791
Needle, you were the only person to vote for me.
I appreciate that.

126
00:05:20,791 --> 00:05:21,958
You can come in, too!

127
00:05:21,958 --> 00:05:22,958
What about us?

128
00:05:22,958 --> 00:05:24,583
Yeah, you can come in too.

129
00:05:24,583 --> 00:05:25,583
Yeah, thanks!

130
00:05:25,583 --> 00:05:27,750
You can pass, you can pass,
you guys can all pass.

131
00:05:28,208 --> 00:05:30,333
Hey, wait, wait, wait! David, I don't know about you.

132
00:05:30,333 --> 00:05:31,791
Aw, seriously?

133
00:05:31,791 --> 00:05:32,916
Okay, go ahead.

134
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:36,666
Flower, I still think you're a jerk
but you can come in.

135
00:05:36,666 --> 00:05:38,458
Wow, Firey, that's so nice of you!

136
00:05:38,458 --> 00:05:40,291
You'd better let me in, or else!

137
00:05:40,291 --> 00:05:43,291
No! Are you serious? Think of all the
things that you've done!

138
00:05:43,291 --> 00:05:46,875
But that's just it. I've grown closer to you
than anyone you've ever known!

139
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:50,250
I mean, if there's anyone who should be let
into the island, it should be me!

140
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:52,666
Y-you're right! Get in there Coiny!

141
00:05:52,666 --> 00:05:54,750
Wow, Firey, tha-that was... that was amazing!

142
00:05:55,041 --> 00:05:56,875
On another note, I can't wait to see Dream Island.

143
00:05:56,875 --> 00:05:58,500
Well, Leafy, I don't think I can let you in.

144
00:05:58,625 --> 00:06:00,916
What!? But you let everybody else in, even Coiny!

145
00:06:00,916 --> 00:06:03,208
Leafy, when you rode my ferris wheel, you said...

146
00:06:03,291 --> 00:06:04,083
Get me outta this thing!

147
00:06:04,083 --> 00:06:05,791
That really hurt me; deep down inside.

148
00:06:05,791 --> 00:06:06,916
You better be joking, Firey!

149
00:06:06,916 --> 00:06:08,291
Leafy, you don't understand!

150
00:06:08,291 --> 00:06:09,833
That ferris wheel, I made it for myself,

151
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:12,708
but more importantly I made it for you
and you just rejected it.

152
00:06:12,708 --> 00:06:13,750
Firey, I don't believe this!

153
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:15,708
Leafy, I'm sorry, but now I see the truth.

154
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:19,541
You are a mean person, and I do not believe
you deserve to be on Dream Island.

155
00:06:22,458 --> 00:06:23,666
Announcer, give me Dream Island!

156
00:06:23,666 --> 00:06:27,333
Ooh, Dream Island is expensive.
Are you able to afford it?

157
00:06:27,333 --> 00:06:29,708
Oh! U-uh, nyuh-huh... Yeah!

158
00:06:30,541 --> 00:06:33,208
Wow! This will help pay for our budget.

159
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:36,666
That should do it.

160
00:06:36,916 --> 00:06:39,000
Huh- uhh, what is going on? Where is Dream Island?!

161
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,541
We had to sell it because of budget slicings.

162
00:06:41,541 --> 00:06:43,625
- Everyone: Ahhhh!
- David: Aw, seriously?
- Blocky: Did you just say that?

163
00:06:43,625 --> 00:06:47,333
Seriously, Speaker Box. You can't just sell Dream Island!

164
00:06:47,333 --> 00:06:47,875
I did.

165
00:06:47,958 --> 00:06:50,500
What?! Guys, we have to get Dream Island back!

166
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:55,250
According to my imagination, 99.8% of
all islands are destroyed within 2 hours of being sold.

167
00:06:55,250 --> 00:06:58,916
Yeah, face it, Pen. We're not
getting Dream Island back.

168
00:06:58,916 --> 00:07:00,708
But... 2 years of battling!

169
00:07:00,708 --> 00:07:01,958
Pen, 2 years is nothing.

170
00:07:01,958 --> 00:07:02,791
Get over it already!

171
00:07:02,791 --> 00:07:06,000
Am I really the only person who wants
Dream Island? At all?

172
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,250
I want Dream Island.

173
00:07:07,250 --> 00:07:09,458
Finally! See? Eraser has a brain.

174
00:07:09,458 --> 00:07:11,125
But erasers don't have brains.

175
00:07:11,125 --> 00:07:12,375
I want Dream Island too!

176
00:07:13,750 --> 00:07:17,333
OMG, why don't we just, like, find out who
got Dream Island right now?

177
00:07:17,375 --> 00:07:20,666
Yeah! Hey Announcery, who did you sell Dream Island to?

178
00:07:20,666 --> 00:07:21,833
I 'an't tell you that.

179
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:22,583
Please!

180
00:07:22,583 --> 00:07:22,958
No,

181
00:07:22,958 --> 00:07:23,791
Please!

182
00:07:23,791 --> 00:07:24,166
No.

183
00:07:24,166 --> 00:07:28,125
If you won't tell me, I'm gonna cry, and I cry acid!

184
00:07:28,125 --> 00:07:31,458
Ha, ha. 'lever. I mean 'unning.
I mean 'rafty. I mean-

185
00:07:31,458 --> 00:07:33,000
Hey, where's Leafy?

186
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,833
Firey, don't tell me you rejected
Leafy from Dream Island!

187
00:07:35,833 --> 00:07:38,166
Ahh... Oh my gosh, look! It's a UFO!

188
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,250
I'm not falling for that trick.

189
00:07:40,083 --> 00:07:44,708
Tennis Ball, Match, Snowball, and Woody:
Ahhhhhh!

190
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:46,166
U-uhm...

191
00:07:47,583 --> 00:07:49,000
Hey guys, I'm back!

192
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,416
H-Hello? Excuse me, where's the celebration?

193
00:07:51,416 --> 00:07:52,958
Flower, I'm tired of this.

194
00:07:52,958 --> 00:07:53,875
Wha-what do you mean?

195
00:07:53,875 --> 00:07:55,708
I mean, I'm tired of your self-centeredness.

196
00:07:55,958 --> 00:07:57,583
I'm tired of the way you act around us.

197
00:07:57,583 --> 00:07:59,333
You know what that means? I'm tired of YOU!

198
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:03,291
- Gasp! Bubble!
- Flower, your unpopularity is your own fault.

199
00:08:03,291 --> 00:08:06,625
Everyone hates you because we can't
stand how you talk only about yourself!

200
00:08:06,625 --> 00:08:08,500
Okay, if that's the way you want to be, fine.

201
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:10,166
If you don't want me, I don't want you!

202
00:08:10,166 --> 00:08:10,875
Wait, what?

203
00:08:11,416 --> 00:08:12,708
Oh, Flower, what are you doing?!

204
00:08:12,708 --> 00:08:14,250
Bubble, you should've seen this coming.

205
00:08:15,291 --> 00:08:16,958
Bubble:
F-Flower, you need to calm down!

206
00:08:17,041 --> 00:08:18,916
Bubble, I'm sorry. Oh wait, I'm not.

207
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:23,583
Oh, and it turns out that that was the
last Bubble Recovery Center. Ever.

208
00:08:23,583 --> 00:08:25,833
Flower, you are an evil person!

209
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:28,875
If that's how you're gonna treat
others then I think you need punishment.

210
00:08:30,083 --> 00:08:31,791
Firey, you do not kill a flower!

211
00:08:32,208 --> 00:08:33,250
How does that feel?

212
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:35,958
So...

213
00:08:35,958 --> 00:08:38,666
OMG, we can play Spongy Cake!

214
00:08:38,666 --> 00:08:41,708
Uh, I don't know what that is,
but it sounds pretty dumb.

215
00:08:41,708 --> 00:08:48,000
Aren't any of you concerned about the fact
that we're in an Unidentified Flying Object?

216
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:51,666
Okay, TB, take a chill pill.
First off, it isn't unidentified.

217
00:08:51,666 --> 00:08:52,208
What?

218
00:08:52,333 --> 00:08:55,791
Match is right. It says the
"Announcer Transportation Device."

219
00:08:55,791 --> 00:08:57,541
And second, it's not flying.

220
00:08:57,541 --> 00:08:59,666
What do you mean? Of course it is!

221
00:09:00,708 --> 00:09:01,791
Not anymore.

222
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,750
Everyone:
Ahhhhh!

223
00:09:05,083 --> 00:09:07,541
Teardrop, help me find out who has Dream Island!

224
00:09:07,541 --> 00:09:08,541
- Can I?
- Sure!

225
00:09:08,541 --> 00:09:10,625
- I'll help as well.
- So where do we start?

226
00:09:10,625 --> 00:09:13,166
Let's ask Leafy. She's on the
other side of the gate.

227
00:09:15,041 --> 00:09:17,208
Leafy, do you have Dream Island?

228
00:09:17,208 --> 00:09:17,625
No?

229
00:09:17,791 --> 00:09:20,791
Firey really needs that island. He deserves it!

230
00:09:20,791 --> 00:09:23,041
Leafy:
I have to disagree with that.
The way he acted was just...

231
00:09:23,541 --> 00:09:24,250
...Wonderful!

232
00:09:24,583 --> 00:09:24,875
Bul-

233
00:09:28,625 --> 00:09:32,833
Match, flip the switch back! Start flying again!

234
00:09:33,041 --> 00:09:36,000
I can't! It's like a one-way lever or something!

235
00:09:36,375 --> 00:09:38,625
There's all the other Announcers!

236
00:09:38,750 --> 00:09:39,166
No way.

237
00:09:41,791 --> 00:09:43,541
Finally! No more vomit!

238
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:43,958
Bleh!

239
00:09:44,666 --> 00:09:46,583
Ice Cube? Uh, not worth it.

240
00:09:47,958 --> 00:09:49,583
Flower! You've got to stop!

241
00:09:49,583 --> 00:09:51,416
Yeah, Flower, end this immediately!

242
00:09:51,583 --> 00:09:56,083
Wow, that's the first time you two have ever
agreed without arguing... I think.

243
00:09:57,208 --> 00:09:58,375
Gah! Bleh...

244
00:09:58,541 --> 00:10:01,625
Has Flower finally stopped her evil doings?

245
00:10:01,625 --> 00:10:02,166
Nope!

246
00:10:03,583 --> 00:10:07,666
I really don't know why Firey would do that.
It seems he turned from a nice caring friend into jerk!

247
00:10:07,666 --> 00:10:09,791
A hideous, unloving jerk with no feelings at all!

248
00:10:09,875 --> 00:10:12,750
Leafy, I know you're upset, but that
doesn't mean you have to call him names!

249
00:10:12,750 --> 00:10:16,458
Maybe we can talk about it?
You know, to soothe your feelings!

250
00:10:16,541 --> 00:10:18,166
Sorry, Pin, I don't want to talk right now.

251
00:10:18,166 --> 00:10:22,000
I know Firey excluded you from Dream Island,
but don't worry about it too much!

252
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:22,916
- Especially because-
- I know,

253
00:10:22,916 --> 00:10:24,750
especially because Firey never
received Dream Island at all.

254
00:10:24,750 --> 00:10:25,916
Wait, how do you know that?

255
00:10:27,333 --> 00:10:28,750
Urh, I heard him talking through the wall.

256
00:10:28,875 --> 00:10:30,916
But isn't that wall soundproof?

257
00:10:32,041 --> 00:10:33,500
I think I know whats going on.

258
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:36,500
You BOUGHT Dream Island, didn't you?
That's how you know everything!

259
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:39,916
This is all your fault, isn't it? Firey rejected you,
you wanted revenge!

260
00:10:39,916 --> 00:10:42,666
Isn't that what happened? Admit that's what happened,
Leafy! Admit it already!

261
00:10:44,333 --> 00:10:46,708
Eraser:
Guys, do you see that? She's turning evil!

262
00:10:46,708 --> 00:10:47,291
Ice Cube:
Wha?

263
00:10:47,291 --> 00:10:48,458
Pin:
What? That's crazy!

264
00:10:48,458 --> 00:10:51,583
I think it's time to see what's really going on
inside this so-called Leafy!

265
00:10:51,583 --> 00:10:52,125
Yeah!

266
00:10:52,583 --> 00:10:53,666
Eraser:
Football?!

267
00:10:53,666 --> 00:10:54,625
I didn't mean that literally!

268
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:59,458
[Everyone protesting]

269
00:10:59,458 --> 00:11:02,041
Here goes that last and most
important recovery center!

270
00:11:06,083 --> 00:11:07,625
I think my work here is done!

271
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:09,333
Don't you realize what you just did?!

272
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:10,750
All the damage you caused?!

273
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:12,958
Now if anyone dies, they'll be gone FOREVER!

274
00:11:12,958 --> 00:11:14,166
And that's what I want!

275
00:11:14,166 --> 00:11:17,041
Bubble, you were nice to me
sometimes but not enough times,

276
00:11:17,041 --> 00:11:19,000
and to be honest I'm not
sad to see you go.

277
00:11:19,416 --> 00:11:20,166
Everyone:
Gasp!

278
00:11:20,250 --> 00:11:20,958
Who's next?

279
00:11:20,958 --> 00:11:23,916
Flower, calm down!
Do you really want to do this?!

280
00:11:23,916 --> 00:11:26,041
Yes, of course I want to do this! That's why I-

281
00:11:26,750 --> 00:11:27,625
What is going on?

282
00:11:27,625 --> 00:11:30,250
Hey guys! OMG, I'm alive!

283
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,958
Yeah, but you killed someone else
under your massive machine.

284
00:11:32,958 --> 00:11:35,541
Oh my gosh, is it Pencil?
It better not be Pencil!

285
00:11:35,541 --> 00:11:36,375
It's Flower.

286
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:37,375
Well that's good then!

287
00:11:38,458 --> 00:11:40,250
Tennis Ball, where's Woody?

288
00:11:40,250 --> 00:11:43,250
- He died.
- Yeah, we did crash pretty hard.

289
00:11:43,250 --> 00:11:45,791
No, he died long before we landed.

290
00:11:45,916 --> 00:11:48,708
Tennis Ball:
His fear of the color grey gave him a heart attack.

291
00:11:50,916 --> 00:11:54,708
We're glad you managed to recover the
funds we've lost during this campaign.

292
00:11:54,791 --> 00:11:58,291
It's proven unsuccessful,
and now it's time to come home.

293
00:11:58,291 --> 00:12:00,833
- But what about-
- It's okay, we can always return.

294
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:08,916
Hey peoples! A meteorite just hit Rocky,
so he can't barf anymore.

295
00:12:09,041 --> 00:12:11,250
Wow, that's amazing!

296
00:12:11,375 --> 00:12:14,000
Where's Leafy? I want to apologize for excluding her!

297
00:12:14,125 --> 00:12:15,875
She didn't deserve to be treated that way.

298
00:12:15,875 --> 00:12:18,666
Well, it turns out that Leafy isn't
such a nice person after all.

299
00:12:18,916 --> 00:12:21,416
Golf Ball:
Leafy was the one who bought Dream
Island so none of us could have it.

300
00:12:21,416 --> 00:12:22,208
Everyone:
Gasp!

301
00:12:22,208 --> 00:12:24,666
I think Leafy deserves the death penalty!

302
00:12:24,666 --> 00:12:25,958
Everyone:
Yeah!

303
00:12:26,208 --> 00:12:29,666
I found Flower's Announcer Crusher!
I'm pretty sure it will do the job!

304
00:12:29,666 --> 00:12:31,291
Wow! Good job, Pencil!

305
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:33,750
Any last words, Leafy?

306
00:12:33,750 --> 00:12:34,375
Yeah, I-

307
00:12:35,791 --> 00:12:37,291
Everyone:
Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill-

308
00:12:37,291 --> 00:12:39,458
Hey, like, what's that thing over there?

309
00:12:39,750 --> 00:12:40,125
Gasp!

310
00:12:40,791 --> 00:12:42,791
What are you doing? Get your
hands off of me you jerk!

311
00:12:42,791 --> 00:12:46,291
Leafy, Leafy! Leafy, I'm sorry for what I did.

312
00:12:46,291 --> 00:12:50,041
I realized that what I wanted most wasn't Dream Island.
It's you, your friendship.

313
00:12:50,541 --> 00:12:54,916
I just want you to know that I'm tired of all this
turmoil that's going on, all these conflicts and stuff.

314
00:12:55,333 --> 00:12:58,500
And I'd rather spend my time with you,
whether it's on Dream Island or not.

315
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,375
Really? You mean it?

316
00:12:59,625 --> 00:13:00,774
Hurry up! We have to get back to the execution!

317
00:13:11,083 --> 00:13:16,708
♪ Uhhh-ahhhhhhh! ♪

318
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:22,083
♪ Smaller cap equals less plastic, plastic! ♪

319
00:13:22,083 --> 00:13:23,083
♪ Tong Yang Hi! ♪

320
00:13:23,875 --> 00:13:26,708
♪ I am a banana, yeah! ♪

321
00:13:27,458 --> 00:13:35,916
♪ Ahhhhhhhhhhh! ♪

322
00:13:37,541 --> 00:13:42,750
♪ Warning: A Cap is small part and poses
as a choking hazard particularly for children, yeah! ♪

323
00:13:43,875 --> 00:13:45,458
♪ NEVER SAY NEVER! ♪

324
00:13:47,458 --> 00:13:51,333
♪ Ahhhhhhhhhhh! ♪

325
00:13:52,583 --> 00:13:54,750
♪ Mmmmm... ♪

326
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:57,625
♪ Yeah! ♪

327
00:14:01,291 --> 00:14:02,208
Hey, Match!

328
00:14:02,208 --> 00:14:06,416
Wouldn't it be weird if the very first and
very last spoken words of BFDI were the same?

329
00:14:07,375 --> 00:14:08,291
Yeah!